    "sha": "ae331e43592458a33af30161da23baa01e7611e2",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOUZ19ENoAKGFlMzMxZTQzNTkyNDU4YTMzYWYzMDE2MWRhMjNiYWEwMWU3NjExZTI",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Gabe Zimbric",
        "email": "10481275+gzimbric@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-10-09T06:03:48Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Gabe Zimbric",
        "email": "10481275+gzimbric@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-10-09T06:05:47Z"
      },
      "message": "server: Add an in-process synchronization backend for macOS.\n\nImplement upstream's in-process sync interface, which so far only has a\nLinux ntsync implementation, on top of a shared-memory region and\nos_sync_wait_on_address. The server owns one region holding every event,\nsemaphore and mutex and one wait block per thread, and hands clients its\ndescriptor in place of a device descriptor; objects are addressed by\nindex with a per-slot generation, so a stale index fails with\nSTATUS_INVALID_HANDLE instead of touching another object.\n\nOne wait-on-address lock in the region header guards the state. It\nrecords its holder's pid so a waiter can recover it if the holder died,\nand is handed to one waiter at a time on unlock. A blocking thread\nregisters its wait block on each object and sleeps on the block's state\nword; whoever makes an object available claims it for the oldest\neligible waiter under the lock, so wait-all is atomic, pulses reach only\nthreads already waiting and a timeout cannot race a signal. Mutexes a\nthread holds are chained under its wait block and released by the server\nwhen the thread dies; kill_thread retires the block before SIGQUIT.\n\nWhen no wait block is available the wait falls through to the server,\nwhose inproc_sync object reads and claims the shared state under the\nsame lock; a client that signals an object with server-side waiters\nsends one wake_inproc_sync request. The region is mapped through\nvirtual_map_host_region as a system view so it never collides with an\napplication allocation.\n\nEnabled by starting the server with STRATUM_SYNC=1; otherwise server\nsynchronization is used. os_sync_wait_on_address is weakly imported, so\non macOS older than 14.4 the server prints one line and keeps server\nsynchronization. This changes the server protocol, so the server and all\nnative modules must be built from the same tree.",
