      "committer": {
        "name": "Gabe Zimbric",
        "email": "10481275+gzimbric@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-10-09T06:05:47Z"
      },
      "message": "winemac: Keep a window's Metal view until its last swap chain releases it.\n\nCount the swap-chain clients of a window's Metal view and detach the\nCAMetalLayer delegate when the last one goes away, instead of removing\nthe view at once. Removal and release are deferred to the main queue so\nthat blocks already queued by the Metal HUD, which retain the layer's\ndelegate view and need its window, run before the view is gone.\nDisposing a content view that still holds a Metal view takes the same\ndeferred path.",
      "tree": {
        "sha": "c418442e1546bfb1ddbe4d9a7a7ada917adb4c9a",
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/gzimbric/wine-arm64-macos/git/trees/c418442e1546bfb1ddbe4d9a7a7ada917adb4c9a"
